BEGIN:VCALENDAR
VERSION:2.0
PRODID:-//Littoralicious//Terroir Athens//EN
X-WR-CALNAME:Athens — eat & drink checklist
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:athens-liste-1@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Kalamaki — The bare pork skewer off the charcoal\, eaten from the stick with a quarter of grilled pita.
DESCRIPTION:Say: ka-la-MA-kee. In Athens the stick is the kalamaki and the souvlaki is the whole wrap: the reverse of Thessaloniki. Best: Elvis\, Kerameikos — order by the pair
LOCATION:Elvis\, Kerameikos — order by the pair
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Elvis+Plataion+29+Athens
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:athens-liste-2@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Souvlaki me ap' ola — Pork in a soft pita with chopped tomato\, onion and a red sauce\, wrapped in paper and eaten standing.
DESCRIPTION:Say: soo-VLA-kee meh ap-OH-la. The wrap is post-war Athenian\; the oldest counter on Agia Irini has sold it since 1946. Best: Kostas\, Plateia Agias Eirinis — before the meat runs out
LOCATION:Kostas\, Plateia Agias Eirinis — before the meat runs out
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kostas+Plateia+Agias+Eirinis+Athens
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:athens-liste-3@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Gyros — Marinated pork slices stacked on a vertical spit\, shaved thin so each serving has a burnt edge.
DESCRIPTION:Say: YEE-ros. The spit came with the 1922 refugees as doner\; Athens made it pork and named it 'the turn'. Best: Hoocut\, Plateia Agias Eirinis
LOCATION:Hoocut\, Plateia Agias Eirinis
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Hoocut+Plateia+Agias+Eirinis+Athens
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:athens-liste-4@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Kebab\, Monastiraki — Hand-formed lamb-and-beef mince grilled as a cylinder over charcoal\, laid on pita with onion and paprika.
DESCRIPTION:Say: keh-BAP. Since 1964 one corner of Mitropoleos has fought a kebab war with the house across the street. Best: O Thanasis\, Mitropoleos 69
LOCATION:O Thanasis\, Mitropoleos 69
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=O+Thanasis+Mitropoleos+69+Athens
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:athens-liste-5@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Paidakia — Thin lamb chops\, charred at the edges\, eaten with the fingers and cold retsina.
DESCRIPTION:Say: pay-DHA-kya. The plate three of this city's chefs named\, separately\, for their own night off. Best: To Steki tou Ilia\, Thissio
LOCATION:To Steki tou Ilia\, Thissio
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=To+Steki+tou+Ilia+Thessalonikis+7+Athens
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:athens-liste-6@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Soutzoukakia smyrneika — Oval meat rolls with cumin\, garlic and wine-soaked bread\, simmered in tomato and allspice.
DESCRIPTION:Say: soo-dzoo-KA-kya smeer-NAY-ee-ka. Smyrna's dish\, carried to Athens by the refugees of 1922. Best: Taverna tou Oikonomou\, Troon\, Ano Petralona
LOCATION:Taverna tou Oikonomou\, Troon\, Ano Petralona
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Taverna+tou+Oikonomou+Troon+41+Athens
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:athens-liste-7@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Pastourma — Air-cured beef under a rust-red crust of fenugreek\, garlic and paprika\, sliced paper-thin.
DESCRIPTION:Say: pa-stoor-MAS. An Armenian refugee from Kayseri began curing it in 1922\; his grandsons still do\, on the same street. Best: Miran\, Evripidou 45 — vacuum-packed for the galley
LOCATION:Miran\, Evripidou 45 — vacuum-packed for the galley
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Miran+Evripidou+45+Athens
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:athens-liste-8@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Lahmajun — Paper-thin dough under spiced minced beef\, rolled hot with greens\, sumac and lemon.
DESCRIPTION:Say: lah-ma-DZOON. Antioch by way of Istanbul\, at a Psyrri counter since 2014: the city's refugee story told again in dough. Best: Feyrouz\, Karori 23\, Psyrri
LOCATION:Feyrouz\, Karori 23\, Psyrri
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Feyrouz+Karori+23+Athens
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:athens-liste-9@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Patsas — Tripe soup\, white and scalding\, sharpened at the table with garlic steeped in vinegar.
DESCRIPTION:Say: pa-TSAS. The market porters' dawn fuel and the city's sworn cure for the night before. Best: Oinomageireio I Ipeiros\, inside the Varvakios
LOCATION:Oinomageireio I Ipeiros\, inside the Varvakios
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Oinomageireio+Epirus+Varvakios+Athens
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:athens-liste-10@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Magiritsa — Lamb offal and lettuce with dill and spring onion\, bound with egg and lemon.
DESCRIPTION:Say: ma-yee-REE-tsa. Eaten once a year\, after the midnight Resurrection\; one market cook-house serves it on ordinary days. Best: Oinomageireio I Ipeiros\, Varvakios
LOCATION:Oinomageireio I Ipeiros\, Varvakios
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Oinomageireio+Epirus+Varvakios+Athens
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:athens-liste-11@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Koulouri — A thin bread ring rolled in sesame and baked hot\, the walking breakfast of the working city.
DESCRIPTION:Say: koo-LOO-ree. Almost every downtown cart loads at one Psyrri bakery before sunrise. Best: To Koulouri tou Psirri\, Karaiskaki 23
LOCATION:To Koulouri tou Psirri\, Karaiskaki 23
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=To+Koulouri+tou+Psirri+Karaiskaki+23+Athens
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:athens-liste-12@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Tyropita kourou — A half-moon of crumbly butter-and-yogurt dough round barrel feta\, eaten warm.
DESCRIPTION:Say: tee-RO-pee-ta koo-ROO. Kourou is from the Turkish for 'dry': not phyllo\, the city's own morning pie. Best: Ariston\, Voulis 10 — before noon
LOCATION:Ariston\, Voulis 10 — before noon
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Ariston+Voulis+10+Athens
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:athens-liste-13@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Loukoumades — Yeast fritters fried to a crisp shell\, drowned in honey syrup and cinnamon.
DESCRIPTION:Say: loo-koo-MA-dhes. The tale that they were prizes for Olympic victors is in no surviving text\; the shop culture is real. Best: Krinos\, Aiolou 87
LOCATION:Krinos\, Aiolou 87
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Krinos+Aiolou+87+Athens
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:athens-liste-14@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Bougatsa — Hand-opened phyllo round custard\, mince or cheese\, buried in icing sugar and cinnamon.
DESCRIPTION:Say: boo-GA-tsa. Thessaloniki's pastry\, which Athens imports: here it is best when the bars have just shut. Best: Bougatsadiko I Thessaloniki\, Plateia Iroon
LOCATION:Bougatsadiko I Thessaloniki\, Plateia Iroon
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Bougatsadiko+I+Thessaloniki+Plateia+Iroon+Athens
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:athens-liste-15@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Galaktoboureko — Semolina custard baked in buttered phyllo and soaked in lemon syrup while hot.
DESCRIPTION:Say: ga-lak-to-BOO-reh-ko. Its home was the milk-shop of the pre-espresso city\; one is left. Best: Stani\, Marikas Kotopouli 10
LOCATION:Stani\, Marikas Kotopouli 10
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Stani+Marikas+Kotopouli+10+Athens
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:athens-liste-16@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Horiatiki — Tomato\, cucumber\, green pepper\, onion\, olives\, a slab of barrel feta\, oregano and oil. Never lettuce.
DESCRIPTION:Say: hor-YA-tee-kee. The one canon dish Athens invented\, in the Plaka tavernas of the 1960s and 70s\; no village was involved. Best: Skalakia\, Ilisia\, with the grill
LOCATION:Skalakia\, Ilisia\, with the grill
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Skalakia+Dionysiou+Aiginitou+32+Athens
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:athens-liste-17@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Retsina — Savatiano white with Aleppo-pine resin added in fermentation\, drunk cellar-cold.
DESCRIPTION:Say: ret-SEE-na. The resin is fixed by law between 0.15 and 1 per cent: in the revival bottles it reads as herb. Best: Domaine Papagiannakos\, Markopoulo — the Retsina of Mesogaia
LOCATION:Domaine Papagiannakos\, Markopoulo — the Retsina of Mesogaia
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Domaine+Papagiannakos+Markopoulo+Attica
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:athens-liste-18@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Tsipouro — A spirit distilled from grape pomace\, with or without anise\, ordered by the karafaki with mezedes.
DESCRIPTION:Say: TSEE-poo-ro. It keeps the fruit that ouzo\, a re-distilled neutral spirit\, does not. Best: Skalakia\, Ilisia — the house tsipouro to open
LOCATION:Skalakia\, Ilisia — the house tsipouro to open
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Skalakia+Dionysiou+Aiginitou+32+Athens
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:athens-liste-19@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Ouzo — Neutral spirit re-distilled with anise\, turned milk-white by water or ice.
DESCRIPTION:Say: OO-zo. EU law reserves the name for Greece and Cyprus. Best: Dexameni\, Kolonaki — at the plane-tree tables
LOCATION:Dexameni\, Kolonaki — at the plane-tree tables
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Dexameni+Kolonaki+Athens
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:athens-liste-20@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Ellinikos kafes — Powder-fine coffee boiled slowly in a briki\, served with its foam and the grounds left to settle.
DESCRIPTION:Say: el-lee-nee-KOS ka-FES. Order it sketos\, metrios or glykos: the sugar goes in the pot\, never after. Best: Mokka\, Athinas 44 — on hot sand
LOCATION:Mokka\, Athinas 44 — on hot sand
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Mokka+Athinas+44+Athens
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:athens-liste-21@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Mastiha — The resin of the Chios lentisk tree: chewed raw\, or as a liqueur and sweets.
DESCRIPTION:Say: MA-stee-ha. Only the mastic villages of southern Chios can make the tree weep\; the know-how is on UNESCO's list. Best: Mastihashop\, Panepistimiou 6
LOCATION:Mastihashop\, Panepistimiou 6
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Mastihashop+Panepistimiou+6+Athens
END:VTODO
END:VCALENDAR
